  "explanation": [
    "The queue gives at-least-once delivery with visibility timeouts: a job a crashed runner never finished reappears for another runner.",
    "Store job state transitions (queued → running → done) with conditional writes so two runners can't both claim a job.",
    "Delayed jobs use a time-ordered index or scheduled messages; a dead-letter queue catches jobs that keep failing."
  ]
